<h2>Sources, references and use</h2>
<p>This dossier is based on:</p>
<p>Lloyd Taylor, Rosamond Georgina. <em>Galapagos Diary</em>. Transcription, edition and notes by Edgardo Civallero. Santa Cruz, Galápagos: Charles Darwin Foundation, 2020. <em>Memorias de la FCD</em>, 1. ISBN 978-9978-53-071-9.</p>
<p><a href="https://www.darwinfoundation.org/en/resources/publications-of-the-library-archive/galapagos-diary/">Read the English edition at the Charles Darwin Foundation</a>. A <a href="https://www.researchgate.net/publication/372566435_Diario_de_Galapagos">Spanish edition translated and edited by Civallero</a> is also publicly available.</p>
<p>Page references throughout this dossier follow the printed pagination of the 2020 English edition. References concerning expedition activities point to Georgina’s diary as transcribed in that edition. Information about the notebook’s physical characteristics, the identification of its author and the preparation of the published text comes from Civallero’s introduction and editorial notes.</p>
<p>The dossier offers an interpretation of selected passages from this publication. It does not incorporate a new examination of the manuscript or comparisons with surviving specimens, collection registers or expedition correspondence. The documentary connections proposed in the closing section are questions for further investigation.</p>
